473234} :answer-field/id #uuid "706d3a7f-ac71-5f66-9b96-e64e194462fb" :answer-field/key "Y" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474012}] :question/id #uuid "c0fa1b96-0701-5539-993f-8523f6af2e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-68745" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $S$ is a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. Also, all the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nNotice that $S$ is not an identity matrix since the diagonal entries are not all ones.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $Y$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, ${y}_{31}=1\\ne 0$).\n\nTherefore, only $S$ is a diagonal matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e161a0e-393f-58cb-a973-4eeec17c7df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509671} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe667f0-2009-50c7-90be-ba73faaf4108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509671} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f49a99-533a-55f6-b257-231b7086c47d" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} 